entityDescription:
SPICI srl &ndash; Company for Innovation, Cooperation and Internationalization, is a Hub for innovation that, operating as an international accelerator and center for entrepreneurship, designs and supports entrepreneurial development, intergovernmental programs for scientific cooperation, technology transfer and internationalization for startups, university spinoffs and innovative SMEs, and develops digital transformation solutions for enterprises and public administration.
SPICI is an active and interconnected part of the ecosystem of knowhow, digital academies and scientific infrastructures of the Technological Pole of the University of Naples Federico II and within this highly valued context, SPICI provides advanced services for the Italian and European industrial and research system (in particular for startups and SMEs), which include scouting, acceleration, digital innovation, technology transfer, finance for growth.
Leveraging on the extensive and consolidated experience of the founders, SPICI works to encourage the attraction in Italy and Europe of capital, talents and innovative projects, providing specialized consultancy and financing guidance services.
SPICI operates both, directly and through its partners on the entire life cycle of startups, from the business conception phase to development on international markets, supporting teams and companies in the process of:
&middot; information and guidance on business creation and entrepreneurial training;
&middot; animation and scouting of new business ideas and management of pre-incubation and acceleration programs;
&middot; accompanying the creation and development of businesses through tutoring, mentorship, coaching, team building, business development and management of incubation and co-working spaces;
&middot; accompanying access to risk finance (venture capital, business angel);
&middot; support for patenting and technology transfer;
&middot; support for the development of digital transformation solutions;
&middot; access to internationalization programs and initiatives.

SPICI, with the aim of supporting companies and public administrations in the process of digital transformation, operates its division FabriTech. It acts as a technological laboratory for the development of digital products &mdash; including softwares, mobile and web apps and physical products &mdash; and related organizational solutions which impact on the way the organization operates internally and within the market.
SPICI has managed several programs related to business acceleration, among these, there is the &ldquo;CHINA-ITALY BEST STARTUP SHOWCASE - ENTREPRENEURSHIP COMPETITION&rdquo; the bilateral platform aimed at promoting the internationalization of Italian and Chinese innovative enterprises (startups, spinoffs, SMEs) that offers the opportunity to get close, approach, do business and land in the two Countries and to meet investors, incubators, science parks and partners through an intense and qualified networking activity.
